---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Projects & Experience - Pavel Kleisner">

    <section class="page-intro">
        <h1>Projects and experience</h1>
        <p class="lead">Long-lived platforms, production integrations and a few tools of my own.</p>
        <div class="body">
            <p>Client systems are private, so instead of screenshots here is what I owned on each, which constraints mattered and what the work taught me. The thread through all of it: understand the domain, make the smallest safe change and stay for what happens after the deploy.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Client work</h2>
        <p class="sub">All through a long-term collaboration with DataLite since 2017, first as an employee, for the last several years as an independent contractor.</p>

        <article class="project">
            <div class="project-head"><h3>TSM / CETIN</h3><span class="when">2020 – now</span><span class="role">senior backend and integration engineer, team lead</span></div>
            <div class="project-body">
                <p>My main long-term focus: backend and integration work on a modern service management platform for a telco operator. I work close to production, on releases, B2B communication with partners, process rules and data compatibility.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Led the production rollouts of versions 2.2 and 2.4, core developer on 1.5.</li>
                    <li>Integration flows around ticketing, NIP, change management, B2B and PEW.</li>
                    <li>Incident analysis from logs, metrics and the data, not blind patching.</li>
                    <li>As the main developer for our part of the platform, a lot of planning, explaining and code review.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="stack"><b>Stack:</b> Kotlin, Java, Spring, PostgreSQL, Kafka, Kubernetes</p>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
            <div class="project-head"><h3>Nordic web</h3><span class="when">2024 – now</span><span class="role">on demand</span></div>
            <div class="project-body">
                <p>Ad-hoc collaboration on a Django-based web system. The volume is low these days, but the engagement stays open and I jump in when there is a focused change to make.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Self-service and web behaviour in Python, Django and templates.</li>
                    <li>Targeted changes in an existing codebase without forcing my usual patterns onto it.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="stack"><b>Stack:</b> Python, Django, templates</p>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
            <div class="project-head"><h3>MNCP</h3><span class="when">2018 – 2021</span><span class="role">full-stack engineer</span></div>
            <div class="project-body">
                <p>Full-stack project around measurement, archives, exports and operational workflows. This is where I moved from delivering features to owning behaviour across backend, frontend and database.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Authentication, export fixes, archive filters and measurement batch behaviour.</li>
                    <li>Database scripts and deployment concerns alongside the application code.</li>
                    <li>Learned to follow a bug through the whole request and data flow, not just one layer.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="stack"><b>Stack:</b> Kotlin, Spring, Angular, Oracle, PostgreSQL</p>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
            <div class="project-head"><h3>ZIS</h3><span class="when">2017 – 2018</span><span class="role">enterprise Java</span></div>
            <div class="project-body">
                <p>An enterprise application for CETIN operations. Java and ZK screens, controller, service and DAO layers, imports, Excel processing and production defects.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Complete business screens from the UI down to persistence.</li>
                    <li>A classic enterprise stack with strict process and data constraints.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="stack"><b>Stack:</b> Java, ZK, ZUL, Maven, SQL</p>
        </article>

        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1.5rem">Before DataLite I worked as a software tester at GMC Software (now Quadient) in Hradec Králové, writing use cases and test scenarios and running the team's Jenkins server.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Own projects</h2>
        <p class="sub">Smaller things I build and run myself, mostly together with AI agents. They keep me close to the whole loop: an idea, a usable interface, data, deployment and maintenance.</p>
        <div class="side">
            <article>
                <h3>Parcel pickup map</h3>
                <p>Every parcel pickup point and box in the Czech Republic on one map, around 40,000 of them, imported daily from carrier feeds and deduplicated.</p>
                <p class="stack">Next.js, PostgreSQL, Drizzle, Leaflet</p>
            </article>
            <article>
                <h3>Family portal</h3>
                <p>Self-hosted apps on a small home server: meal plans with real nutrition data, a planner for everything around the house, trips and packing lists.</p>
                <p class="stack">Next.js, Drizzle ORM, PostgreSQL, Raspberry Pi</p>
            </article>
            <article>
                <h3>Trading bot</h3>
                <p>A trend-following strategy (EMA crossover, ATR stop) for testing assumptions against market data, not for selling certainty.</p>
                <p class="stack">Python, Freqtrade</p>
            </article>
            <article>
                <h3>This website</h3>
                <p>Static, bilingual, cheap to run and easy to change. The source is on GitHub.</p>
                <p class="stack">Astro, TypeScript, Cloudflare Pages</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta bleed">
        <h2>Want to talk about a project?</h2>
        <a class="email" href="mailto:contact@pavelkleisner.dev">contact@pavelkleisner.dev</a>
    </section>

</Layout>
